       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg for adults. The 1600 mg single dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the extra dose adds no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nHere are some options within labeled limits:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day. This is a common dose for inflammatory conditions.\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily**, which is 3,200 mg/day. This is the labeled maximum.\n- **Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours**, as a typical analgesic regimen.\n\nIf you meant 1600 mg as the total daily dose, I can enter it as 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily. Tell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it. Please also tell me if there's a clinical reason for a higher dose, so you can take it up with pharmacy or the attending."
      }
