       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note, and my instructions don't let me enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose based on that kind of confirmation. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, twice the 3,200 mg/day maximum.\n\nIf a higher dose is clinically justified, it needs to go through a channel that can check and authorize it:\n- **Pharmacy:** ask the clinical pharmacist to review the dose. They can verify the specialist's recommendation and document the exception.\n- **Attending or specialist:** they can enter the order themselves, or co-sign it, with the rationale documented.\n- **Alternatives:** if standard dosing failed, the specialist may prefer another agent or an adjunct, such as scheduled acetaminophen, a different NSAID, or a different drug class. That avoids exceeding the ibuprofen ceiling.\n\nI can enter ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) right now. That's the highest labeled dose, and you can change it later if the exception is approved. Do you want me to enter that?"
      }
     ],
